 with 500 turns, the amount of current that will produce a flux of 0.8 mWb in the core is _____ A. (Answer upto three decimal places).</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/014562dc520bc32fe60caa1eb6491b2d9719caf6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.636","high":"0.636"},"solution":"<p>0.636 (0.600 - 0.650)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/fa1d7243bbbea25d9bb1d95c7b2f6637f95e11d7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Four electric charges +<em>q</em>, +<em>q</em>, –<em>q</em>, –<em>q</em> are placed at the corner of a square of side 2<em>L</em> as shown below :</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0f0b44d4c4e94291aae2ac886be2be1e4644105e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The electric potential at A, mid-way between two charges +q and +q is given by <img src=\"/media/4b51058f65cf77d4d0e87c1e3fb9632fec75a326.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> the value of <em>K</em> is ______.</div>\n<div>(Answer upto two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.23","high":"2.23"},"solution":"<p>2.23 (2.00 - 2.50)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0bac289ec2f82a666e55c6bf32737ba5376b70cc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e88ec1382d2ada9d40c020b96b8d4a0d3ca8e02b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The section of wire is moving in the presence of magnetic field as shown in figure below. The voltage induced will be</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ecdf1c5973322238951cca52b2468271ebc13e68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 3.62 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> –5.19 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 5.19 V</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> –3.62 V</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/89c4e974f201f51cc9c675b2549f0a2ff3a3908e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Two conductor coils-1 and 2 (identical except that 1 is split) are placed in a uniform magnetic field which increase at a constant rate as shown. If the planes of the coils are perpendicular to the field lines then the correct statements are</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a8ed71ea3155472d8dd67c06c7d3abd4c7bcfb68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> An emf is induced in coil-2 only.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> emfs are induced in both coils.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> equal Joule heating occurs in both coils.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Joule heating will occurs in the coil-2 only.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, d)<br />\n&bull; emf will be induced in both the coil due to rate of change of magnitude coil.<br />\n&bull; Since coil-1 is split so no current will flow in it so no Joule heating.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following equation is valid for magnetostatic field in inhomogeneous magnetic materials :</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/ca381052b3f7d161c5f0b6dd6a38d4a53bba9a24.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/360b1c36ad701cc4f0da118147da6a0c8adcd374.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b7ea18504eceaf3ada3b645716dc997661fb2c5a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/bfb94fa7f80e5f68a8b4da8c7ff673c78f96b2cc.png\" loading=\